[Music]  6 43 here on a wednesday morning time  now for our mornings with metro segment  and today we're joined by assistant  sheriff laz chavez to answer your  questions and our questions this morning  how are you doing sir good to see you  very good thanks for coming in thank you  let's start talking about something that  we've been seeing recently it's not  necessarily a new issue but it certainly  got a lot more attention on social media  recently street racing drifting around  the valley  what kind of reports are you seeing  around town what's being done to try and  stop these things from taking place yeah  well what we've seen is it is it's a bit  of a national trend now too but we're  mostly focused on the northeast side of  the valley and over on the northwest  side of the valley these these reckless  drivers they take over intersections  they drive around circles they videotape  each other it's a dangerous uh element  of the for the general public so we're  responding out there as quick as we can  and we're working with community  partners  we try to get video of people doing this  and help identify some of these drivers  and these stunt drivers i remember at  the beginning of the pandemic we had  covered this a lot more because there  were fewer people on the streets and so  there was a lot of more folks were  taking advantage of that by drifting  around and and so forth  how quickly can you get out there i mean  it's not like those folks are taking  part are going to say hey rather we're  drifting out in near nellis uh how  quickly can you get out there and how  much of an emphasis is it well you'd be  surprised a lot of times this does go  out on social media so we try and stay  ahead of that we can get our helicopter  out there very quickly  and we work closely with community we  get a lot of phone calls so we respond  as fast as we can  we work with uh with surveillance video  a lot of times and we were able to  apprehend a few suspects that were out  there doing this stuff okay well keep an  eye on that let's switch gears to the  coronavirus and sadly  another sad situation with metro two  more officers have died recently from  covid19 we've spoken with the sheriff  about this before and others with the  department what is the latest with  vaccinations and cases within metro  police yeah that is sad and and tragic  and our prayers go out to the family uh  for their loss but for metro about 56  percent of our employees now have gotten  the first shot we're moving in the right  direction it's not quite where we want  to be uh we're following the governor's  uh mandate uh officers are wearing masks  and we're providing uh lots of  opportunity for them to get their  vaccine and even doing some pop-ups at  some of the police stations i know in  the beginning there was i don't know if  it was hesitancy but there was you know  there are union rules about mandating  vaccines for staff uh how is the  department and some of the brass trying  to not necessarily get around that but  try and make sure that everyone stays  safe while still making sure you follow  the the rules of the the contract well  that that is that is a hurdle that we're  dealing with we're trying to work with  the unions and uh and accommodate our  employees we we do provide as much as we  can uh to them and information we're on  this almost weekly try and encourage our  employees civilians and our commissioned  officers to to get the vaccine okay  well with vaccine mandates in place uh  across up and down the strip at some of  our large venues one of the concerns  that seems to be coming up is fake  vaccine cards what can you do what can  investigators do to make sure that when  folks are trying to get in they really  haven't vaccinated that's gonna be a big  issue moving forward along the strip too  of course yeah and and it's really  difficult at this point it's so early on  we're looking at our other law  enforcement agencies across the country  they're dealing with this we actually  haven't received very many calls at all  about this uh it's it's difficult you  know what do you do to verify these  cards do you call the hospitals to  verify the shots or not so we're asking  folks please be cautious of that if you  falsify a document you could be looking  at some different charges there too it's  not like if you're going to a legion  stadium to watch a raiders game you have  a fake vaccine card that you can just  call someone like there's that's that's  an instant kind of decision that has to  be made whether it's it's good or not  right right exactly exactly and in the  stadiums and that events are requiring  shots but that's certainly private  property they can make those decisions  on their own and we will do everything  we can as this moves on to try to figure  out how's the best approach for that it  is a gargantuan task for metro for  everybody else assistant sheriff chavez  thank you for joining us this morning we  really appreciate answering our  questions if you have a question for  metro police you can as always submit it  on 8newsnow.com we love hearing from you  as well find out if your question is  answered every wednesday during mornings  with metro 6

